    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10386" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιπολέμιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>warring against,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἀντιπολέμιοι</span>”
				<i>enemies,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.90
				</span></i>
			 codd. (but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πόλεμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					1.150
				</span></i>
			); in <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.134
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				140
			</span></i>, codd. vary between <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιπόλεμοι</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-μιοι;</span>
			but in <i><span class="en">
				7.236
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				8.68
			</span></i>.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β́ ἀντιπόλεμοι</span> occurs
			without v.l., and is the only form cited by <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Onos.
				10.9
			</span></i>,al.</div>
